meta {
  name: End Household Membership
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/households/{{householdId}}/members/{{householdMemberContactId}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

tests {
  test("returns 200 OK", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });

  test("reports the membership as ended", function () {
    expect(res.getBody().ended).to.equal(true);
  });

  test("ends the membership of the member Add Household Member just created", function () {
    // The pairing is what keeps this collection re-runnable against one
    // database: the member added a moment ago is removed again, so a second run
    // does not grow the household by another Dana Tyson.
    expect(bru.getVar("householdMemberContactId")).to.be.a("string");
  });
}

docs {
  # DELETE /households/:id/members/:contactId

  End a membership — **"remove from household"**, on the Household Details page
  (`/clients/:id`).

  - **Module:** `clients` (the class-level OR-gate also accepts `crm_service`
    for the **reads** on this controller; this write does not).
  - **Permission:** `clients:write`.
  - **Data scope:** the household is loaded through the same scope filter as
    `GET /households/:id` — `own` collapses to branch on client records. Out of
    scope reads as 404.

  ## Why this is a DELETE on the *membership*, not on the contact

  Membership is a join collection since PAC-91 §5 (`householdMembers`), because
  a contact can belong to several households and the two facts that matter here
  belong to the **pair**: the role in this household, and when it ended.

  So the person is untouched. They keep existing, they keep every other
  household they belong to, and they keep appearing on this household's
  historical policies, deals and tickets. Only the link stops.

  ## Soft, not removed

  The row stays and `endedAt` is stamped. "Was a driver here until March" is a
  fact a service rep needs, and the `$pull` from an array this replaces left
  nothing behind at all. Re-adding the same person later revives the same row
  rather than inserting a second one.

  A second call therefore finds no **current** membership and returns **404** —
  the row is still there, but there is nothing left to end.

  ## The primary contact cannot be removed

  A household whose `primaryContactId` names somebody who is not a member of it
  is a state no reader can render sensibly, so the request is refused with
  **409**. Assign a different primary contact first — a deliberate operation of
  its own (PAC-91 §7).

  ## Response
  `{ "ended": true }`

  ## Errors
  | Status | When |
  |---|---|
  | 401 | Missing/expired bearer token |
  | 403 | `clients` disabled for the agency, or the caller lacks `clients:write` |
  | 404 | Unknown household or contact, a malformed id, a household outside the caller's scope, or no current membership to end |
  | 409 | The contact is the household's primary contact |
}
